# UI specification (islands)

## Required

1. Before changing UI chrome, layout, colours, radii, or spacing: read `GUARDRAILS.md` and `docs/design/islands/SPEC.md`.
2. Reuse layout constants from `crates/app-ui-kit/src/layout.rs` and palette / `theme::` helpers from `crates/app-base/src/theme.rs`. No new gap, radius, or product-chrome hex literals outside that scale.
3. Allowed surfaces: island, dialog, popover/menu, call window, toast. A new surface type updates `docs/design/islands/SPEC.md` in the same change (and the feature OpenSpec that needs it).
4. Feature OpenSpecs describe content and behaviour on those surfaces; they do not invent look tokens.

## Do not

- Invent parallel spacing or radius numbers in views
- Hard-code raw hex for product chrome in views (change the palette / scheme instead)
- Add a new shell band or primary island slot without extending the islands SPEC
- Grow radius drift (3 / 4 / 8 / 12); when touching such a file, move toward 6 or 10
